-# SmoothMotion 2.8.5 RTX20/RTX30 Fix 27 — DX12 games adopted at Present, better flow
+# SmoothMotion 2.8.5 RTX20/RTX30 Fix 28 — Vulkan, and objects that stay whole
+
+- **Vulkan games are supported** (e.g. Red Dead Redemption 2 in Vulkan mode).
+  - The module registers itself as a Vulkan layer for the game's process only.
+    Nothing is installed system-wide.
+  - Same optical flow, synthesis and pacing as DX11/DX12.
+  - Requirements:
+    - Load it through `version.dll` or an ASI loader, as for DX games.
+    - Do not run the game as administrator.
+  - `Vulkan=0` turns it off.
+- **Fewer fragments in camera turns.** NVIDIA's optical flow drags thin or
+  small objects (helmet crests, sword tips, heads) to the camera's motion and
+  blends motions across their outlines. Synthesis tore such objects apart.
+  - The flow is now checked against the frames first, and such vectors are
+    replaced by the motion of a nearby cell that actually matches.
+  - In the new test of a thin crest over a 20-pixel pan, wrong crest pixels
+    fell from 252 to 25 (blended flow) and from 146 to 56 (dragged flow).
+  - `FlowRefine=0` turns it off.
+- `Test\RTX20_VulkanLayerTest.exe` checks the Vulkan path on your PC.
+
