+# Fix28 validation and limits
+
+Fix28 adds Vulkan presentation (a per-process Vulkan layer with a D3D11
+bridge) and two flow refinement passes (13 HLSL entries,
+artifact_guard=occlusion_aware_v12).
+
+**Vulkan layer**
+
+- **Linux (`source/rtx20/test_vulkan.py`).** The layer core with a
+  pure-Vulkan stand-in generator, loaded by the real loader under Mesa
+  lavapipe and the Khronos validation layer. Six cases: immediate and FIFO;
+  applications asking for Vulkan 1.0, 1.1 and 1.2; with and without a Vulkan
+  1.2 features chain. Each: 120 frames, 120 captures, 118 generated and 120
+  real presents, 0 validation errors (validation/rtx20-vulkan-layer.json).
+- **Wine 9.0** (optional `--vulkan-wine-loader`). The built normal.asi with
+  the Khronos Windows loader v1.3.275 (built from source with
+  LOADER_USE_UNSAFE_FILE_SEARCH, because Wine processes are elevated) and
+  winevulkan:
+  - Registration, manifest discovery, the Win32 dispatch chain, Vulkan 1.0
+    raised to 1.1 and every frame presented.
+  - A child process in another folder loads the module as a forwarding
+    layer only.
+  - With the release loader, the module correctly reports that the loader
+    ignores it in an elevated process.
+  - winevulkan has no Win32 external memory, so the D3D11 bridge did not run.
+
+**Shaders**
+
+- The suite has 27 groups, passing in optimized and ASan/UBSan builds.
+- New crest group, wrong crest pixels Fix27 -> Fix28:
+  - dragged: 146 -> 56
+  - blended: 54 -> 26
+  - blended over a wide band: 252 -> 25
+  - noisy: 133 -> 46
+  - blended and noisy: 179 -> 81
+- Other groups:
+  - Unchanged or better: crosshair baseline core 75 -> 111, translucent
+    crosshair core 42 -> 47, half-resolution parallax 28 -> 23, exposure +25%
+    161 -> 156.
+  - Exposure +15% parallax: 79 -> 87.
+  - Smeared silhouette: 417 in total either way.
+- Real Witcher 3 triplets: wrong pixels lower in all ten cases (block
+  matcher standing in for NVOF).
+- All 13 entries compile with d3dcompiler_47 (O3, no warnings).
+
+**Not tested**
+
+Nothing ran on Windows with an NVIDIA GPU:
+
+- the D3D11-Vulkan interop;
+- NVOF on Vulkan frames;
+- displayed output;
+- the GPU cost of the refinement passes (estimated 0.2-0.6 ms per pair at
+  1080p).
